  "honest-render/src/honest_render/_util.py:constant_replace \"\"\"The if-free branch primitive, a private copy of honest-observe's _util (honest-observe section 3):\nhonest-render passes its own checker, so its source carries no `if` statement, ternary or comprehension\nfilter (HC-P001). A branch is a boolean key computed and a thunk looked up in a closed two-row table\n(P01). These are plain names bound to lambdas, not `def`s, so they add no column-0 function to the\nmodule's declared set -- every declared function keeps its one gherkin scenario and nothing else does.\n\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=0, column=0)-Point(row=5, column=3)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-render/src/honest_render/render.py:constant_replace \"\"\"Hand the .hd source text to honest-design's read_hd and resolve its Document to exactly one\n    Module (section 3b). On a one-module Document it returns that bare Module; on a zero- or\n    multi-module Document it returns the client not_single_module Fault as data, its detail stating the\n    module count; on a read_hd fault it passes that bare Fault through unchanged (recognized by\n    is_fault). honest-render never parses .hd itself; this pull is the only way it obtains a Module.\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=114, column=4)-Point(row=118, column=103)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-render/src/honest_render/render.py:constant_replace \"\"\"Hand the Module to honest-design's render and return the four-column Diagram it drew, unchanged.\n    honest-render never recomputes column placement or edges; this pull is the only way it obtains the\n    layout. honest-design's render is total and reports no fault.\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=124, column=4)-Point(row=126, column=68)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-render/src/honest_render/render.py:constant_replace \"\"\"honest-render: the public static renderer of one .hd declaration.\n\nRead the file, get honest-design's Module and Diagram, build a ViewModel, render Markdown, write it\nout. Read-only and deterministic; it never parses .hd and never recomputes layout. I/O lives at the\nboundaries (read_source, the two import seams read_ir/draw_diagram, write_document); the pure core\n(build_view, render_markdown, render_fault) takes data and returns data. Faults travel in the return\nvalue as a bare union arm (value | Fault), never raised.\n\nSection builders and renderers are selected in declaration order through tables. Their pure\nhelpers build view sections and Markdown without reaching outside the given inputs.\n\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=0, column=0)-Point(row=10, column=3)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-render/src/honest_render/render.py:constant_replace \"\"\"Assemble one honest-render Fault record from its four parts. The reserved is_err tag is always\n    true, and code/category/message/detail are carried through unchanged. Pure: it reads no world.\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=50, column=4)-Point(row=51, column=101)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
