  "honest-render/src/honest_render/render.py:constant_replace \"\"\"Turn honest-design's Module and Diagram into a ViewModel: the declaration reorganized into the\n    order and groupings a reader wants. It decides structure, not text, and invents nothing the\n    declaration does not state. Column placement and edges come from the diagram; every other fact\n    comes from the module. Pure: it reads no world.\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=345, column=4)-Point(row=348, column=54)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-render/src/honest_render/render.py:constant_replace \"\"\"Render one numbered Markdown item per chain line or route or entry row.\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=383, column=4)-Point(row=383, column=81)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-render/src/honest_render/render.py:constant_replace \"\"\"Turn the ViewModel into the Markdown document string: the module heading and note as prose, a\n    function shown whole as prose, the types/sets/vocabularies/dispatches as tables, the\n    chains/routes/entries as lists. Deterministic: the same ViewModel renders to byte-identical\n    Markdown every time, with no clock and no external state. Pure: it reads no world.\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=415, column=4)-Point(row=418, column=89)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-render/src/honest_render/render.py:constant_replace \"\"\"Write the document to exactly one side, chosen by output.path: a path string writes to that file\n    (file:given), NOTHING (None) writes to standard output (stdout). Thin: it builds no Fault. ok true\n    with empty detail on a clean write; ok false with the write error in detail on a failure. The side\n    choice is a two-row table on whether path is NOTHING, not an if (HC-P001); the handle closes within\n    the with-scope (stdout stays open via nullcontext), and the OS error is caught here and reported as\n    data, never a raise.\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=440, column=4)-Point(row=445, column=27)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-render/src/honest_render/render.py:constant_replace \"\"\"Compose the work above the pure core and own all fault construction. Pull the file text; on a\n    failed read build a file_unreadable client Fault via render_fault. On a clean read pull the Module\n    (read_ir) and, when it is a Fault -- either a passed-through read_hd fault or the client\n    not_single_module fault read_ir built -- pass it through unchanged and render nothing (section 3b).\n    Otherwise draw the diagram, drive the two pure steps, and write; on a failed write build a\n    write_failed server Fault. On a clean write return the document string. Every fault comes back as\n    data, never raised; each decision is a closed two-row table (P01).\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=474, column=4)-Point(row=480, column=73)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
  "honest-render/src/honest_render/render.py:constant_replace \"\"\"The single input boundary, the one door honest-render presents. It accepts a RenderRequest and\n    hands it to exactly one orchestrator, render_declaration, adding nothing of its own. It returns the\n    rendered document string on success, or honest-render's Fault as data when the render failed. The\n    fault travels back here by return; the door is never where it is raised.\"\"\"->\"\"@Point(row=519, column=4)-Point(row=522, column=79)": "The mutation changes only a Python docstring. The module contract does not depend on introspected documentation text, and the executable syntax is identical.",
